WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.070 --> 00:02.320
Looks like your bad luck finally wore off.

3
00:02.670 --> 00:04.000
I'm the one stuck with it now.

4
00:04.050 --> 00:07.430
I told you already. You are meant to live as one.

5
00:07.710 --> 00:10.180
The heaven and earth do not acknowledge your love.

6
00:10.270 --> 00:11.630
You're here early...

7
00:16.070 --> 00:19.030
If you want to keep staying at my place, you're welcome to.

8
00:19.060 --> 00:20.230
I'd rather not.

9
00:20.730 --> 00:22.930
I don't want to be a third wheel to you.

10
00:23.170 --> 00:24.110
For now,

11
00:24.750 --> 00:27.020
I'll stay with Nadol.

12
00:36.980 --> 00:37.780
Oh?

13
00:38.970 --> 00:39.770
Hey!

14
00:41.690 --> 00:42.880
Come on, Hunglay.

15
00:48.320 --> 00:50.640
Jeez, what's wrong with you all of a sudden?

16
00:53.420 --> 00:54.680
Is the spark plug acting up?

17
01:00.090 --> 01:01.310
I already told you

18
01:01.500 --> 01:03.300
that you can still stay at my place.

19
01:04.390 --> 01:05.530
I'd rather not.

20
01:06.210 --> 01:08.220
The couch in Nadol's room is perfectly fine.

21
01:08.780 --> 01:10.780
You'll end up with a sore back if you sleep on a couch.

22
01:11.810 --> 01:12.980
My back is doing alright.

23
01:13.860 --> 01:15.160
I'm not as old as you are.

24
01:16.920 --> 01:17.920
According to our contract,

25
01:18.590 --> 01:20.320
you're supposed to stay at my house.

26
01:21.000 --> 01:22.400
Do you even remember what's in it?

27
01:24.040 --> 01:25.400
Our roles as husbands, you know.

28
01:26.700 --> 01:27.900
You're funny, Inspector.

29
01:28.560 --> 01:30.080
You keep reminding me about the contract.

30
01:31.210 --> 01:32.710
What about the promise you made?

31
01:33.220 --> 01:35.070
You said you'd be a faithful husband.

32
01:36.820 --> 01:37.950
Do you remember that?

33
01:38.220 --> 01:39.820
I just want you to have a good life,

34
01:40.160 --> 01:41.770
like I promised your mom.

35
01:41.910 --> 01:43.330
I'm doing just fine right now.

36
01:43.740 --> 01:45.240
It's you changing your mind all the time

37
01:45.260 --> 01:46.380
that's making things difficult.

38
01:47.650 --> 01:49.170
You might want me around today,

39
01:50.030 --> 01:52.840
but you might push me away tomorrow.

40
01:54.680 --> 01:55.930
What exactly do you want?

41
02:07.450 --> 02:09.650
Can I give you a piece of advice, Inspector?

42
02:11.170 --> 02:14.730
There are psychiatrists here in Chiang Mai.

43
02:16.380 --> 02:18.240
I think you should go see one.

44
02:19.040 --> 02:21.080
They might know why you keep changing your mind.

45
02:38.230 --> 02:39.520
No, thanks.

46
02:40.400 --> 02:41.400
Come on.

47
02:57.860 --> 02:59.240
It's started now, so get off.

48
03:36.160 --> 03:39.140
(Yin as Theartha)

49
03:44.070 --> 03:46.800
(War as Mungkorn)

50
03:50.940 --> 03:53.290
(Shane as Phuwin)

51
03:53.720 --> 03:56.760
(Boss as Lukplub)

52
03:59.140 --> 04:00.870
(Kit as Kanin)

53
04:01.130 --> 04:03.080
(Tang as Nadol)

54
04:06.560 --> 04:11.800
(Tae as Saming)

55
04:56.620 --> 04:57.460
Mungkorn.

56
04:58.120 --> 04:59.010
Lady Pharada?

57
05:00.000 --> 05:00.940
Hello.

58
05:02.180 --> 05:03.480
Is something the matter?

59
05:03.780 --> 05:04.690
Yes, of course.

60
05:05.250 --> 05:06.820
I'm here to bring you back home.

61
05:07.140 --> 05:09.320
Thear told me you haven't been home for two days.

62
05:09.640 --> 05:10.600
What happened?

63
05:13.600 --> 05:14.790
It's nothing.

64
05:16.280 --> 05:18.850
I just moved back to where I belong.

65
05:19.880 --> 05:23.100
The police flats are the right place for me.

66
05:24.530 --> 05:27.750
A junior officer shouldn't be staying at his superior's house.

67
05:30.820 --> 05:31.690
Mungkorn,

68
05:32.520 --> 05:35.170
I care about you like you're my own son.

69
05:35.990 --> 05:37.320
Tell me the truth.

70
05:38.400 --> 05:39.840
You're not coming home...

71
05:40.380 --> 05:42.350
because of Thear and Belle, right?

72
05:47.340 --> 05:49.480
Do you actually have feelings for my son?

73
05:53.490 --> 05:55.620
If you tell me that you don't,

74
05:56.480 --> 05:58.320
I'll let you stay here.

75
06:01.020 --> 06:02.800
But if the truth is...

76
06:03.440 --> 06:05.240
you do have feelings for him...

77
06:09.040 --> 06:11.100
you have to be honest with me, dear.

78
06:20.820 --> 06:21.620
I do.

79
06:23.120 --> 06:24.620
I think I'm in love with Inspector Thear.

80
06:24.640 --> 06:26.000
Then take him back!

81
06:26.620 --> 06:28.730
Stop acting like you're his second choice.

82
06:28.780 --> 06:29.980
You're his only choice.

83
06:30.000 --> 06:30.880
Why would you let her win?

84
06:30.900 --> 06:35.200
You are his legally wedded spouse in every sense.

85
06:35.340 --> 06:37.240
So, what should I do?

86
06:37.780 --> 06:40.380
Their old spark is burning so brightly.

87
06:41.540 --> 06:43.090
I'll teach you.

88
06:43.250 --> 06:47.180
Believe it or not, I'm the president of the Wives Club.

89
06:50.110 --> 06:50.910
Alright.

90
06:51.230 --> 06:52.610
It's time to call him yours

91
06:52.630 --> 06:54.270
and take him back.

92
07:06.950 --> 07:09.080
When are you heading back to the States?

93
07:09.420 --> 07:11.080
Probably in a week or two.

94
07:11.420 --> 07:13.430
Once you've got everything sorted out,

95
07:13.530 --> 07:14.920
it'll probably be just about time.

96
07:17.820 --> 07:19.100
Just let me know, then.

97
07:19.130 --> 07:21.820
In the meantime, make yourself at home.

98
07:29.320 --> 07:30.360
Who's that?

99
07:49.160 --> 07:50.330
Oh, honey?

100
07:50.640 --> 07:51.580
Belle?

101
07:52.600 --> 07:53.720
You're back?

102
07:54.820 --> 07:56.100
Wanna swim with me?

103
07:56.180 --> 07:57.060
I'm good.

104
07:57.200 --> 08:00.400
I didn't bring a swimsuit with me.

105
08:01.990 --> 08:03.640
What about you, honey?

106
08:06.120 --> 08:07.460
Aren't you going to join me?

107
08:08.490 --> 08:10.760
I thought you weren't coming home.

108
08:11.420 --> 08:13.240
I wasn't going to,

109
08:14.180 --> 08:16.200
but like you said, honey...

110
08:17.160 --> 08:19.140
I have to be here to take care of you.

111
08:19.880 --> 08:21.640
After all, that's what a husband should do.

112
08:22.220 --> 08:23.680
Having someone else do it...

113
08:24.040 --> 08:25.540
wouldn't be right.

114
08:26.640 --> 08:27.950
Don't you agree, Belle?

115
08:29.950 --> 08:30.750
Yeah.

116
08:35.040 --> 08:37.620
Are you really not going to join me?

117
08:50.940 --> 08:52.200
It's hot today.

118
08:54.190 --> 08:55.730
Should we do something "cool" together?

119
08:57.250 --> 08:58.120
I'm good.

120
08:58.630 --> 09:01.090
I'm not in the mood for a swim.

121
09:01.670 --> 09:03.370
Then what are you in the mood for?

122
09:03.920 --> 09:05.140
I can join you.

123
09:06.660 --> 09:09.260
I'm pretty tired today. I just want to rest.

124
09:09.910 --> 09:11.500
Let's go, Belle.

125
09:27.570 --> 09:29.130
How is it going, Mungkorn?

126
09:29.570 --> 09:31.470
They went up to Belle's room together.

127
09:32.470 --> 09:33.490
What are they doing in there?

128
09:34.270 --> 09:36.510
I don't know. They were holding hands, too.

129
09:36.840 --> 09:37.680
Hey!

130
09:37.890 --> 09:39.780
Don't you want to find out?

131
09:40.300 --> 09:41.260
I do.

132
09:41.290 --> 09:42.620
Then you have to find out.

133
09:43.230 --> 09:44.780
What do you want me to do?

134
09:48.520 --> 09:51.920
Khaopuk, how is a nosy maid supposed to act?

135
09:53.620 --> 09:55.120
When we wanna know something,

136
09:55.140 --> 09:57.320
we'll pry until we find out.

137
09:57.640 --> 10:00.050
We have every right to know the truth.

138
10:05.250 --> 10:06.450
Are we really doing this?

139
10:06.480 --> 10:08.390
Well, if you're curious, you've got to know.

140
10:08.420 --> 10:11.190
Remember, she thinks it's special, but it's all reused. Go!

141
10:11.610 --> 10:12.680
- Good luck. - Go on, dear.

142
10:14.470 --> 10:15.260
Go, go!

143
10:19.410 --> 10:21.430
- Whoa, it's high! - Just go!

144
10:21.680 --> 10:22.970
Good luck, Mr. Mungkorn.

145
10:23.830 --> 10:25.820
Make sure you eavesdrop successfully!

146
10:25.850 --> 10:27.690
Thanks for the support, everyone.

147
10:43.090 --> 10:45.190
How's it going? Are they doing it?

148
10:45.420 --> 10:46.450
Puk, be quiet.

149
10:47.200 --> 10:48.090
You're being too loud.

150
10:59.990 --> 11:01.360
What are you doing up here?

151
11:04.270 --> 11:05.080
Whoops, run!

152
11:05.100 --> 11:05.970
Go!

153
11:10.890 --> 11:11.760
Well...

154
11:12.050 --> 11:14.530
An injured bird got stuck on this balcony,

155
11:15.120 --> 11:16.200
so I came up to help it.

156
11:17.300 --> 11:18.550
Then it flew away.

157
11:19.070 --> 11:20.760
I guess it's not hurt anymore.

158
11:21.230 --> 11:22.920
Seems like I'm the only one who still is.

159
11:23.880 --> 11:25.230
Oh...

160
11:25.850 --> 11:27.370
So you're not afraid of heights anymore?

161
11:28.500 --> 11:29.660
Not anymore.

162
11:30.220 --> 11:31.790
You have to face it until you're used to it.

163
11:37.630 --> 11:40.980
Well, if I see the bird, I'll catch it for you.

164
11:41.550 --> 11:43.130
You're such a kind person.

165
11:44.270 --> 11:45.390
Not really.

166
11:46.850 --> 11:48.970
When I see someone in trouble, I always help them.

167
11:50.720 --> 11:52.870
But somehow, people never see my worth.

168
11:53.810 --> 11:55.510
They just see me as a placeholder.

169
12:07.040 --> 12:08.020
Hey!

170
12:08.510 --> 12:10.500
You're going down that way? Isn't it dangerous?

171
12:20.660 --> 12:22.350
Please allow me to get out of your way.

172
12:49.490 --> 12:50.560
Hey, Mungkorn.

173
12:51.120 --> 12:53.200
Why are you pressing up against me?

174
12:53.440 --> 12:54.460
Go back to your side.

175
12:56.560 --> 12:58.090
But I'm cold.

176
13:00.220 --> 13:03.700
Cuddling my husband is warmer than using a blanket.

177
13:03.970 --> 13:07.370
If you're cold, just turn up the AC.

178
13:08.010 --> 13:09.000
I don't want to.

179
13:10.390 --> 13:12.800
I'd rather do something with my husband...

180
13:13.410 --> 13:15.240
to get warmer.

181
13:45.200 --> 13:46.180
Wait.

182
13:46.720 --> 13:47.830
I'm burning up.

183
13:48.440 --> 13:49.500
I'll sleep outside.

184
13:59.210 --> 14:00.520
Mungkorn,

185
14:00.800 --> 14:02.070
how was last night?

186
14:02.100 --> 14:04.250
Tell me something good.

187
14:04.280 --> 14:08.040
Did you two get intimate under the covers?

188
14:09.530 --> 14:11.010
We didn't do anything at all.

189
14:11.040 --> 14:12.000
Oh?

190
14:12.020 --> 14:14.000
He wouldn't even let me sleep next to him.

191
14:15.210 --> 14:16.580
I'm serious.

192
14:16.880 --> 14:18.610
No matter how much I try to tempt him,

193
14:20.140 --> 14:22.110
it doesn't work if he doesn't want it.

194
14:22.740 --> 14:25.690
Maybe you weren't sexy enough?

195
14:26.450 --> 14:27.510
It's possible, My Lady.

196
14:28.100 --> 14:32.330
Come on, there are still a hundred more ways.

197
14:34.780 --> 14:36.170
Thear, gosh...

198
14:37.560 --> 14:39.790
I guess I'll have to play hardball with him.

199
14:43.810 --> 14:44.760
Thear!

200
14:45.300 --> 14:46.420
Where are you off to?

201
14:49.920 --> 14:50.980
Oh...

202
14:51.550 --> 14:54.620
I'm taking Belle to a waterfall.

203
14:55.260 --> 14:57.000
We're going camping for a night.

204
14:59.230 --> 15:00.900
Oh, that's perfect!

205
15:01.120 --> 15:04.090
Mungkorn is a real nature lover.

206
15:04.120 --> 15:06.930
He loves the planet, the mountains, and everything.

207
15:06.950 --> 15:10.190
He wants to go to the waterfall, too, right?

208
15:12.180 --> 15:12.960
That's right.

209
15:13.610 --> 15:14.790
Take him along with you, son.

210
15:14.810 --> 15:17.220
He's already packed all his stuff.

211
15:17.240 --> 15:18.020
Right, Cupid?

212
15:19.490 --> 15:20.370
Yes, My Lady.

213
15:20.930 --> 15:21.900
Khaomao, Khaopuk!

214
15:22.350 --> 15:23.870
- Yes? Yes! - Yes.

215
15:28.120 --> 15:29.600
What about you, Belle?

216
15:29.640 --> 15:31.710
Do you have anywhere else you want to go?

217
15:31.740 --> 15:34.480
Or are you moving somewhere soon?

218
15:34.500 --> 15:37.250
I mean, how much longer are you planning to stay here?

219
15:38.040 --> 15:40.470
That would depend on Thear.

220
15:42.330 --> 15:44.200
Where do you want her to move to?

221
15:44.670 --> 15:46.780
I asked her to come stay with me.

222
15:46.800 --> 15:48.240
She's staying for the long haul.

223
15:48.270 --> 15:49.840
It'll be easier for me to take care of her.

224
15:52.510 --> 15:56.200
You take such good care of your friend, don't you?

225
15:56.720 --> 15:59.240
But you're terrible at taking care of your husband.

226
15:59.590 --> 16:01.450
Aren't you doing a pretty bad job here?

227
16:05.850 --> 16:10.420
Have you had any aches or pains, Mungkorn?

228
16:11.630 --> 16:12.600
No.

229
16:15.780 --> 16:16.820
That's good.

230
16:17.540 --> 16:20.860
That proves I've been taking pretty good care of him, Mom.

231
16:24.400 --> 16:25.500
Is everything ready, Cupid?

232
16:25.610 --> 16:26.630
I'm tired of waiting.

233
16:26.830 --> 16:29.170
- Khaomao, Khaopuk, hurry up! - Coming.

234
16:30.020 --> 16:31.880
Wait, where's Puk? Puk, move it!

235
16:32.010 --> 16:33.020
Gosh.

236
16:33.270 --> 16:35.220
You're so slow. Keep those feet moving fast.

237
16:35.250 --> 16:37.480
- Hurry. - It's so heavy. What's even in here?

238
16:39.240 --> 16:40.280
Here it is.

239
16:43.130 --> 16:44.980
- Ready for you to be Mowgli now. - Right.

240
16:48.640 --> 16:49.620
Let me help you with your bag.

241
16:52.120 --> 16:52.820
Let's go.

242
16:53.630 --> 16:54.420
Bye, Mom.

243
16:54.630 --> 16:55.820
Have a great trip.

244
16:57.270 --> 16:58.550
What do we do now?

245
16:59.760 --> 17:01.380
Yes, My Lady. Let's go.

246
17:01.990 --> 17:03.350
Go. Hurry up.

247
17:07.530 --> 17:08.550
Lady Pharada,

248
17:09.000 --> 17:10.460
I think I'd better not go.

249
17:11.070 --> 17:12.610
It'll just be awkward for everyone.

250
17:12.640 --> 17:13.700
You must go, dear.

251
17:13.920 --> 17:15.610
I've already paved the way for you.

252
17:17.660 --> 17:22.550
This is what I want to entrust to you before I'm gone.

253
17:23.970 --> 17:26.250
You absolutely cannot give up, Mungkorn.

254
17:26.520 --> 17:27.580
Are you dying?

255
17:27.600 --> 17:28.520
I'm going on a trip.

256
17:30.200 --> 17:32.140
I have a trip with the other police wives.

257
17:51.730 --> 17:53.420
Mungkorn, is there a song you'd like to hear?

258
17:54.600 --> 17:56.060
I'm fine with anything.

259
17:59.300 --> 18:01.160
Then let's go with this one.

260
18:10.920 --> 18:15.720
♪I have a heart to give, when will you receive it?♪

261
18:16.940 --> 18:22.080
♪Can you hear it? My love, can you hear my wishes?♪

262
18:22.740 --> 18:26.010
♪All of my heart...♪

263
18:26.040 --> 18:26.720
Hey.

264
18:27.260 --> 18:29.600
Why? Don't you like this song?

265
18:31.760 --> 18:32.690
It's not that.

266
18:33.260 --> 18:35.190
I don't like listening to music while driving anymore.

267
18:35.450 --> 18:36.640
It's distracting.

268
18:47.620 --> 18:49.950
I'm sorry, Belle, for having to tag along.

269
18:51.190 --> 18:52.930
Lady Pharada forced me to come.

270
18:53.960 --> 18:56.760
It's totally fine. The more, the merrier.

271
18:57.350 --> 19:00.150
She probably wanted you and Thear to spend some time together.

272
19:00.550 --> 19:02.850
If anything, I'm the third wheel here.

273
19:03.530 --> 19:04.600
No, you're not.

274
19:04.810 --> 19:07.510
I wanted to come with you anyway.

275
19:12.960 --> 19:15.340
Honestly, I don't think marriage can change one's luck,

276
19:16.040 --> 19:18.980
but I understand that Thear wanted to put his mom's mind at ease.

277
19:21.360 --> 19:22.500
You don't have to worry.

278
19:22.850 --> 19:25.440
It'll be six months before you know it.

279
19:25.870 --> 19:28.600
By the time you're back next time, I'll be single again.

280
19:30.700 --> 19:32.030
Why are you telling me this?

281
19:32.850 --> 19:34.220
You should care about Mungkorn, too.

282
19:34.250 --> 19:36.820
He's helped you so much, yet you're still being mean to him.

283
19:38.240 --> 19:39.310
How so?

284
19:39.940 --> 19:40.810
Ask him yourself.

285
19:41.010 --> 19:42.740
He's benefiting from this marriage, too.

286
19:43.460 --> 19:44.260
That's right.

287
19:45.500 --> 19:47.590
I'm doing this only for the benefits.

288
19:49.280 --> 19:50.560
Once he's free of me,

289
19:51.680 --> 19:54.130
he can go back to being a playboy just like before.

290
20:11.970 --> 20:13.580
Is your bag heavy? Want me to carry it?

291
20:14.040 --> 20:15.900
It's not. I can carry it.

292
20:19.960 --> 20:21.100
Careful, it's slippery.

293
20:23.340 --> 20:24.860
Let me lead the way.

294
20:27.780 --> 20:29.050
Come on, hold onto me.

295
20:29.450 --> 20:31.130
I'm fine. I can manage. Look.

296
20:31.570 --> 20:34.370
Come on, just listen to me. You might fall and hurt yourself.

297
20:34.910 --> 20:36.520
You don't need to fuss over me.

298
20:36.840 --> 20:37.960
I can take care of myself.

299
20:38.340 --> 20:39.270
I can't help it.

300
20:39.420 --> 20:41.510
I want you to know that I've never changed.

301
20:41.540 --> 20:44.090
When I love someone, I always take the best care of them.

302
20:44.340 --> 20:45.350
It's okay.

303
20:45.520 --> 20:48.100
I'm a modern woman. I can handle myself just fine.

304
20:48.240 --> 20:48.960
Look.

305
20:49.970 --> 20:51.220
Come on, it's dangerous.

306
20:51.240 --> 20:52.320
See?

307
20:54.020 --> 20:55.180
Careful.

308
20:55.210 --> 20:55.950
Okay.

309
21:24.260 --> 21:25.060
Are you okay?

310
21:25.900 --> 21:26.920
I'm fine.

311
21:27.280 --> 21:28.160
Thanks.

312
21:29.130 --> 21:30.430
Watch your step, will you?

313
21:30.780 --> 21:32.760
If you fall, you might end up with amnesia.

314
21:33.300 --> 21:34.440
That might actually be good.

315
21:35.000 --> 21:36.600
There are things I'd like to forget anyway.

316
21:41.060 --> 21:41.930
Wow.

317
21:42.080 --> 21:43.980
The water is so clear. It makes me wanna jump right in,

318
21:44.340 --> 21:46.470
but I'm not going to swim today.

319
21:46.600 --> 21:48.380
Why? We're already here.

320
21:49.240 --> 21:51.160
I'm on my period. It's the first day.

321
21:51.750 --> 21:53.260
You and Mungkorn go ahead and swim.

322
21:53.290 --> 21:54.720
I'll cheer you on from up here.

323
21:57.630 --> 22:00.220
If you're not going to swim, I'm not going to swim.

324
22:00.640 --> 22:02.190
Would you let Mungkorn swim alone, then?

325
22:02.530 --> 22:03.490
It's okay.

326
22:03.960 --> 22:05.470
No need to bother him.

327
22:08.640 --> 22:10.120
Let's hurry up and put our things away

328
22:10.450 --> 22:11.660
so we can finally have fun.

329
22:46.530 --> 22:47.250
Hey!

330
22:47.570 --> 22:48.040
Belle!

331
22:48.060 --> 22:49.510
Whoa, it got in my ear.

332
22:49.640 --> 22:52.070
You're going for it 'cause I can't pull you down, huh?

333
22:53.150 --> 22:54.830
Take that.

334
22:54.850 --> 22:57.420
Mungkorn, help me. This guy needs to be taught a lesson.

335
22:57.440 --> 23:00.040
You're so mean, huh?

336
23:00.490 --> 23:01.720
Fine. You want this?

337
23:04.010 --> 23:05.260
Come on, Mungkorn.

338
23:07.980 --> 23:08.870
Whoa!

339
23:10.070 --> 23:10.870
Hey!

340
23:13.050 --> 23:14.170
Whoa, wait.

341
23:15.530 --> 23:16.690
Isn't that too much?

342
23:16.990 --> 23:18.280
I can even give you more than that.

343
23:19.170 --> 23:19.880
Hey!

344
23:19.960 --> 23:20.590
Whoa.

345
23:21.270 --> 23:22.260
Are you holding a grudge?

346
23:23.280 --> 23:25.040
Don't make this personal.

347
23:25.870 --> 23:27.740
Want me to dunk you, then?

348
23:31.820 --> 23:33.460
You can't beat me. Come on.

349
23:34.220 --> 23:35.180
- Bring it on. - Bring it on.

350
23:35.570 --> 23:36.400
Come on.

351
23:42.670 --> 23:43.630
Stop it.

352
23:48.120 --> 23:49.910
I don't think this is going to work.

353
23:50.190 --> 23:51.970
Having me play the evil ex

354
23:51.990 --> 23:53.770
just to stop Mungkorn's bad luck?

355
23:53.830 --> 23:55.020
I can't bring myself to do it.

356
23:55.210 --> 23:57.080
He's been so good to you.

357
24:01.230 --> 24:02.230
Ugh, I don't care.

358
24:02.250 --> 24:04.730
No matter what, I have to make him hate me

359
24:04.750 --> 24:07.650
so I can take all that bad luck back onto myself.

360
24:07.800 --> 24:10.800
Sure, Mr. Hero, sacrificing everything for love.

361
24:11.220 --> 24:13.080
We never know when our time is up.

362
24:13.110 --> 24:15.020
We deserve to be with the person we love.

363
24:18.540 --> 24:20.780
Otherwise, just get a divorce and end this

364
24:21.520 --> 24:23.010
because what you're doing

365
24:23.240 --> 24:24.940
makes it seem like you don't care about him at all.

366
24:26.800 --> 24:28.130
Yeah, I just...

367
24:29.630 --> 24:32.060
I just want to stay with him a little longer.

368
24:34.110 --> 24:36.020
Whatever, I don't buy it.

369
24:36.670 --> 24:39.360
And you shouldn't let an oracle dictate your life.

370
24:39.380 --> 24:42.280
I saw him get shot right before my eyes, Belle.

371
24:42.470 --> 24:44.350
I didn't believe it at first,

372
24:45.240 --> 24:46.910
but now I'd rather not take any chances.

373
24:47.290 --> 24:49.240
Please forgive her, Heaven and Earth.

374
24:55.490 --> 24:56.910
You love him a lot, don't you?

375
25:00.070 --> 25:00.950
Yeah.

376
25:01.150 --> 25:02.220
It's okay.

377
25:02.830 --> 25:05.880
I'll do whatever it takes to help you through this.

378
25:09.000 --> 25:10.050
Thanks

379
25:11.090 --> 25:14.580
for always loving and caring about me.

380
25:33.360 --> 25:34.800
You're jealous of me and Belle, aren't you?

381
25:35.270 --> 25:36.810
Don't flatter yourself.

382
25:37.240 --> 25:40.000
I'm just doing what Lady Pharada asked me to do.

383
25:40.500 --> 25:41.580
Don't lose your focus.

384
25:42.500 --> 25:43.900
It's only six more months.

385
25:44.380 --> 25:45.500
Is it that unbearable?

386
25:47.500 --> 25:48.300
That's right.

387
25:48.860 --> 25:49.940
It is unbearable.

388
25:50.250 --> 25:52.300
I can't wait to put an end to this.

389
25:53.390 --> 25:55.030
Then just let me go.

390
25:59.060 --> 25:59.940
Let go of me.

391
26:03.600 --> 26:04.680
Inspector...

392
26:05.270 --> 26:06.260
Let me go.

393
26:06.410 --> 26:07.280
Let go!

394
26:09.960 --> 26:10.830
Belle?

395
26:11.810 --> 26:12.780
Where is she?

396
26:13.460 --> 26:14.590
Hey, Belle.

397
26:17.450 --> 26:18.930
I'd better go call her.

398
26:21.060 --> 26:21.810
Belle!

399
26:26.740 --> 26:29.440
(I'm having cramps, so I'm leaving. I'll pick you up tomorrow.)

400
26:30.070 --> 26:31.500
Wow, Belle.

401
26:53.890 --> 26:54.690
What are you doing?

402
26:56.480 --> 26:57.700
Setting up my tent, obviously.

403
27:05.760 --> 27:06.910
No need for that.

404
27:09.090 --> 27:10.340
We'll just sleep in the same one.

405
27:10.550 --> 27:12.080
So you wanna sleep next to me now?

406
27:13.710 --> 27:15.450
You were disgusted with me last night.

407
27:16.300 --> 27:17.430
I wasn't.

408
27:18.830 --> 27:20.100
I was just confused.

409
27:20.910 --> 27:21.910
Confused about what?

410
27:26.920 --> 27:28.620
Confused about...

411
27:29.870 --> 27:31.930
how I should treat you.

412
27:36.360 --> 27:37.560
I was feeling bad for Belle.

413
27:42.090 --> 27:43.050
Okay.

414
27:44.380 --> 27:46.610
In that case, I'll clear up your confusion for you.

415
27:54.540 --> 27:55.260
Wait.

416
27:57.210 --> 27:58.150
Where are you going?

417
27:58.760 --> 28:00.540
To ask the staff to take me home.

418
28:02.800 --> 28:03.690
Don't do that.

419
28:06.200 --> 28:07.620
Can you stay with me tonight?

420
28:13.230 --> 28:14.460
Why would I?

421
28:15.570 --> 28:16.980
In fact,

422
28:17.950 --> 28:19.390
I wasn't even supposed to be here.

423
28:24.560 --> 28:25.740
Things have changed.

424
28:50.930 --> 28:51.900
Want a beer?

425
29:03.110 --> 29:04.430
Do you remember these mugs?

426
29:05.020 --> 29:06.580
I'm still using them, you know.

427
29:18.020 --> 29:19.320
I'll do it myself.

428
29:27.730 --> 29:28.910
Have you put it on yet?

429
29:33.830 --> 29:34.400
Here.

430
29:43.900 --> 29:45.300
It's okay. I'll do it myself.

431
30:03.200 --> 30:05.030
Can I ask you something, Inspector?

432
30:11.170 --> 30:13.170
Belle is such a lovely person.

433
30:15.380 --> 30:18.440
How could you let her slip through your fingers?

434
30:21.770 --> 30:24.330
It's because of my cunning, playboy ways.

435
30:27.020 --> 30:28.880
By the time I was ready to change, it was too late.

436
30:31.460 --> 30:32.820
What if she...

437
30:34.030 --> 30:36.300
gave you a chance?

438
30:37.820 --> 30:39.410
Would you do it for her?

439
30:44.610 --> 30:45.410
I don't know.

440
30:48.290 --> 30:49.520
Someone like me...

441
30:50.150 --> 30:52.850
probably deserves to be punished by fate

442
30:54.400 --> 30:56.080
and be alone for the rest of my life.

443
30:58.220 --> 31:00.200
Whoever I love, I just bring them bad luck

444
31:01.540 --> 31:02.950
and end up breaking their heart.

445
31:08.540 --> 31:09.790
You've only got yourself to blame.

446
31:16.180 --> 31:17.540
I think...

447
31:19.840 --> 31:21.840
there's always a chance to do better.

448
31:23.460 --> 31:25.930
Why keep making the same old mistakes?

449
31:27.470 --> 31:29.500
If you just change and become a new man,

450
31:30.390 --> 31:32.550
I'm sure Belle could fall for you again.

451
31:48.800 --> 31:50.600
But I don't want Belle to fall for me again.

452
32:13.100 --> 32:14.310
I'm going to the bathroom.

453
32:38.950 --> 32:39.830
Mungkorn.

454
32:40.500 --> 32:43.000
Why are you doing it here? Why don't you use the bathroom?

455
32:43.030 --> 32:44.420
Something might snatch you up.

456
32:44.630 --> 32:45.720
There's nothing out here.

457
32:46.470 --> 32:47.570
Why did you follow me?

458
32:47.590 --> 32:50.760
I'm worried about you. What if a tiger takes you?

459
32:51.360 --> 32:52.720
There are no tigers here.

460
32:53.430 --> 32:54.700
This isn't their hunting ground.

461
33:03.810 --> 33:05.250
Sh*t! A snake!

462
33:06.060 --> 33:06.820
Hey, wait.

463
33:06.840 --> 33:07.750
Right there!

464
33:07.780 --> 33:09.750
- It really is a snake. - Yeah, I told you! Go!

465
33:09.850 --> 33:11.440
Go, Mungkorn!

466
33:11.460 --> 33:13.690
Is it gone? Move over here.

467
33:13.710 --> 33:14.820
Are there any more?

468
33:14.850 --> 33:17.760
It's gone, Inspector. It went over there.

469
33:18.320 --> 33:19.400
Jeez...

470
33:21.300 --> 33:22.800
My legs are covered in pee now.

471
33:31.950 --> 33:32.770
Just a stick.

472
33:37.040 --> 33:38.100
For an inspector,

473
33:39.040 --> 33:40.140
you're terrified of snakes, huh?

474
33:40.170 --> 33:41.380
What does my rank have to do with it?

475
33:41.400 --> 33:43.520
I just don't like them. They're gross and slimy.

476
33:45.520 --> 33:47.360
How are you so calm?

477
33:47.530 --> 33:49.370
Snakes get into my house all the time.

478
33:49.400 --> 33:50.430
It's nothing new to me.

479
33:51.430 --> 33:52.930
I could even catch one to show you.

480
33:52.960 --> 33:54.670
No need to go that far.

481
33:56.980 --> 33:59.090
Don't tell anyone about this, okay?

482
34:00.030 --> 34:01.150
It's embarrassing.

483
34:01.930 --> 34:03.450
Nobody else knows about this.

484
34:04.910 --> 34:06.430
I won't tell a soul, Inspector.

485
34:07.330 --> 34:10.140
I'm great at keeping secrets, you know that.

486
34:16.180 --> 34:17.230
Can we go now?

487
34:18.670 --> 34:21.490
It's coming back!

488
34:21.510 --> 34:22.890
What is wrong with you?

489
34:23.260 --> 34:24.720
I'm heading into the tent.

490
34:25.260 --> 34:26.340
It's just a stick.

491
34:40.690 --> 34:42.120
Calm down, Inspector.

492
34:57.520 --> 34:58.520
I've already checked.

493
34:59.120 --> 35:00.290
No snakes around here.

494
35:02.720 --> 35:03.620
Thanks a lot.

495
35:06.020 --> 35:07.060
You should get some sleep

496
35:07.810 --> 35:09.040
so we can leave early.

497
35:11.730 --> 35:12.980
You're the only one

498
35:13.740 --> 35:15.590
who gets to see this side of me.

499
35:17.870 --> 35:20.170
Even Belle has never seen you like this?

500
35:21.120 --> 35:21.880
Never.

501
35:22.460 --> 35:23.760
I can't let anyone else see it.

502
35:24.370 --> 35:26.380
I'm supposed to be the cool inspector.

503
35:26.560 --> 35:27.960
I'm not allowed to be afraid.

504
35:28.270 --> 35:30.220
Always have to be the protector.

505
35:31.520 --> 35:32.980
But since you came along,

506
35:33.860 --> 35:35.850
I can let my guard down.

507
35:38.770 --> 35:41.560
Do you really have to put on an act like that?

508
35:43.310 --> 35:44.300
Doesn't it get exhausting?

509
35:45.910 --> 35:47.420
When you love someone,

510
35:47.790 --> 35:49.900
you should be able to be yourself.

511
35:56.720 --> 35:57.760
I'm heading to bed.

512
36:16.430 --> 36:18.060
I'm sorry for making you upset,

513
36:18.990 --> 36:20.370
but it was necessary.

514
36:35.520 --> 36:36.990
I think I understand.

515
36:40.200 --> 36:41.930
It's just that the timing...

516
36:43.010 --> 36:44.220
is all wrong.

517
36:45.900 --> 36:47.350
If it weren't for me,

518
36:49.140 --> 36:51.880
you and Belle would've gotten back together by now.

519
36:58.030 --> 37:00.030
Should I explain things to Lady Pharada?

520
37:02.060 --> 37:03.240
I'm sure she would understand.

521
37:08.550 --> 37:09.950
Or maybe...

522
37:12.220 --> 37:14.120
your bad luck has finally run its course.

523
37:14.150 --> 37:15.420
It hasn't!

524
37:17.630 --> 37:20.050
(But why is it Mungkorn who's having all the bad luck instead?)

525
37:20.080 --> 37:23.270
I told you already. You are meant to live as one.

526
37:23.290 --> 37:26.260
Yet you have heeded none of my words.

527
37:26.290 --> 37:28.720
The heaven and earth do not acknowledge your love.

528
37:31.980 --> 37:32.690
Here goes.

529
37:33.370 --> 37:36.520
Please, Heaven and Earth, and the spirits of the forest, help me.

530
37:36.620 --> 37:38.210
It probably won't be what I'm thinking.

531
37:39.940 --> 37:40.990
What exactly are you thinking?

532
37:50.780 --> 37:52.360
Wait, Inspector.

533
37:52.910 --> 37:54.360
No more waiting.

534
37:54.380 --> 37:56.820
Please just let me be a good husband for once.

535
39:50.100 --> 39:51.630
If I'd known it would be this good,

536
39:52.720 --> 39:55.750
I would've let you do it from the day we got married.

537
39:58.970 --> 40:00.270
Was it really that good?

538
40:02.690 --> 40:04.680
It was exactly like Lukplub told me.

539
40:06.030 --> 40:07.920
He said it'd feel so warm...

540
40:08.820 --> 40:10.960
like being showered with love from the whole world.

541
40:14.390 --> 40:15.700
You don't need the whole world.

542
40:16.370 --> 40:19.220
Just me alone is more than enough.

543
40:26.710 --> 40:28.090
I'm really happy...

544
40:29.140 --> 40:30.510
that my first time...

545
40:31.570 --> 40:34.210
happened when we actually had feelings for each other.

546
40:44.310 --> 40:45.630
Right, Thear?

547
40:48.720 --> 40:50.590
We did it out of love, didn't we?

548
40:54.010 --> 40:54.840
Of course we did.

549
40:57.300 --> 40:58.820
Everything that happened...

550
40:59.400 --> 41:00.770
and every single touch...

551
41:01.600 --> 41:03.320
came from love.

552
41:20.830 --> 41:24.710
Then let's do another couple activity, shall we?

553
41:26.510 --> 41:27.480
What now?

554
41:38.650 --> 41:39.800
Face masks.

555
41:43.260 --> 41:44.700
Wow, you're really well-prepared.

556
41:54.840 --> 41:55.830
Part your hair.

557
42:36.120 --> 42:37.570
Well, it feels cool.

558
42:38.270 --> 42:39.270
Does it feel refreshing?

559
42:39.990 --> 42:40.930
It does.

560
42:48.270 --> 42:49.180
What are you doing?

561
42:49.210 --> 42:50.870
Setting a timer for 15 minutes.

562
42:54.350 --> 42:55.280
Okay.

563
43:53.290 --> 43:54.520
Is it morning already?

564
43:56.310 --> 43:58.340
I slept so well that I completely overslept.

565
44:01.340 --> 44:02.520
You can sleep a bit longer.

566
44:03.660 --> 44:05.190
The weather's nice and warm.

567
44:05.790 --> 44:06.890
It's perfect for cuddling.

568
44:10.140 --> 44:11.830
Should we stay another night?

569
44:13.690 --> 44:17.260
I don't think anything else will happen.

570
44:18.100 --> 44:19.490
Anything else?

571
44:20.380 --> 44:21.470
What do you mean?

572
44:23.640 --> 44:25.170
Oh, I just mean...

573
44:25.520 --> 44:27.910
there shouldn't be anything to worry about

574
44:28.170 --> 44:29.860
or get in our way,

575
44:30.270 --> 44:31.500
like wild animals.

576
44:31.700 --> 44:33.690
Tigers or snakes, you know.

577
44:34.370 --> 44:35.420
No more.

578
44:36.890 --> 44:39.350
Just some wolf-manizer around here.

579
44:42.190 --> 44:44.410
Wanna see what this wolf can do in the morning?

580
44:44.930 --> 44:45.680
I can do this.

581
44:46.170 --> 44:47.020
And this.

582
44:47.040 --> 44:48.020
Stop it.

583
44:48.040 --> 44:49.140
You're not actually a wolf.

584
44:50.150 --> 44:51.100
I'm a wolf snake.

585
44:51.520 --> 44:52.530
That's a venomous snake.

586
44:52.550 --> 44:53.450
No, it's not.

587
44:55.360 --> 44:56.180
But you are.

588
44:56.370 --> 44:57.890
Good morning!

589
44:57.940 --> 44:58.890
Whoa, Belle!

590
44:59.290 --> 45:00.620
- Belle, can you give us a minute? - Belle...

591
45:01.630 --> 45:02.560
We'll be right out.

592
45:03.490 --> 45:04.740
My bad. I'm sorry.

593
45:04.900 --> 45:06.190
I didn't think you'd go this far.

594
45:32.160 --> 45:33.560
So, everything's settled?

595
45:35.530 --> 45:36.300
Well...

596
45:38.200 --> 45:39.130
It's just as it looks.

597
45:40.910 --> 45:44.710
I told you. We are the ones who decide our own fate.

598
45:47.350 --> 45:49.260
The weather's so refreshing today.

599
45:51.240 --> 45:53.810
Heaven and earth are on our side.

600
46:03.610 --> 46:04.860
Hey, Mungkorn!

601
46:12.020 --> 46:13.160
Are you hurt? Did it hit you?

602
46:14.070 --> 46:14.950
I'm okay.

603
46:15.540 --> 46:16.960
Whoa, that was a close call.

604
46:29.460 --> 46:30.200
Where are you going?

605
46:30.230 --> 46:32.900
To help Captain arrest the Black Bull at the karaoke bar.

606
46:32.930 --> 46:33.690
You can't go.

607
46:33.820 --> 46:35.260
When I give you an order, you follow it.

608
46:35.280 --> 46:36.430
I'm your superior.

609
46:36.650 --> 46:38.120
I really don't know my place.

610
46:38.150 --> 46:40.850
I know full well I'm just meant to ward off his bad luck.

611
46:40.910 --> 46:42.000
A guy like that

612
46:42.030 --> 46:43.560
isn't worth your love.

613
46:43.720 --> 46:45.310
You deserve someone better.

614
46:45.340 --> 46:46.240
If it were me,

615
46:46.260 --> 46:48.030
I would never hurt you.

616
46:48.050 --> 46:49.360
So, you just wanted to sleep with me?

617
46:52.410 --> 46:57.290
♪Trying so hard not to cross the line,♪

618
46:57.320 --> 47:02.150
♪But the more I run, the more you're on my mind♪

619
47:02.170 --> 47:06.440
♪If you're gonna love me, don't break the deal we made♪

620
47:06.470 --> 47:11.930
♪Don't break my heart, remember what you said?♪

621
47:11.950 --> 47:16.960
♪Let's call off the deal and let our hearts decide♪

622
47:16.990 --> 47:23.360
♪From contracting parties to lovers, does that sound alright?♪

623
47:29.690 --> 47:32.860
♪It's time you became mine♪
